---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Unity House Centres — UK Programme" description="Unity House Centres is a proposed UK public-benefit programme being developed by Visio Nova Mundi CIC to test locally adaptable community resource and support models.">
  <section class="heroBlock">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Proposed UK programme · Controlled partner discovery</p>
      <h1>Unity House Centres</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        A proposed UK community resource and support model being developed by Visio Nova Mundi CIC to test how trusted local organisations,
        surplus resources and simple coordination systems could work together to create measurable community benefit.
      </p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="btn primary" href="/contact">Discuss a proposed partnership</a>
        <a class="btn" href="/tree-of-life">See the wider Tree of Life</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <aside class="statusCard">
      <p class="statusLabel">Current status</p>
      <h2>Designed for local adaptation</h2>
      <p>Unity House is being shaped as a repeatable model. Waltham Forest is the proposed first test location, subject to the required partners, controls and evidence.</p>
      <span class="statusPill">No centres currently operating</span>
    </aside>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="sectionHead">
      <p class="eyebrow">How a future local Unity House node could work</p>
      <h2>Local proof first, potential UK replication later</h2>
      <p>
        Unity House Centres is intended to be locally adaptable rather than dependent on one council, borough or building.
        Each proposed node would begin with a real local need and an appropriate host, then be shaped around the resources,
        safeguards and partners available in that place. A permanent centre would only be considered after the hosted model has produced credible evidence.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="flow">
      <div><strong>1</strong><span>One evidenced local need</span></div>
      <div><strong>2</strong><span>One trusted host</span></div>
      <div><strong>3</strong><span>One resource stream</span></div>
      <div><strong>4</strong><span>Appropriate partners</span></div>
      <div><strong>5</strong><span>Responsible coordination</span></div>
      <div><strong>6</strong><span>Evidence and learning</span></div>
    </div>
    <p class="formula">1 evidenced local need + 1 trusted host + 1 resource stream + appropriate partners + Unity House coordination + responsible evidence = 1 testable local Unity House node</p>

    <div class="pilotFlow" aria-label="Proposed local Unity House pilot flow">
      <div><strong>Surplus-food partner</strong><span>Resource is offered through an appropriate partner.</span></div>
      <span class="flowArrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      <div><strong>Trusted local host</strong><span>A suitable venue and local relationship are confirmed.</span></div>
      <span class="flowArrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      <div><strong>Community access</strong><span>People access the support through the host arrangement.</span></div>
    </div>
    <p class="coordinationLine"><strong>Unity House coordinates, records and evaluates.</strong></p>
  </section>

  <section class="grid section">
    <article class="card highlight">
      <p class="eyebrow">Proposed Pilot 01 · Waltham Forest</p>
      <h2>Food is the first test resource stream</h2>
      <p>
        Visio Nova Mundi CIC is beginning locally by exploring a small hosted pilot in Waltham Forest.
        Pilot 01 would test surplus-food redistribution through an existing trusted community venue and specialist partners,
        without operating a new kitchen or presenting the pilot as an active service.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Existing venue rather than new premises</li>
        <li>Partner-led food handling and custody arrangements</li>
        <li>Simple internal register rather than a full production app</li>
        <li>Evidence of what was offered, transferred, used and learned</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="note"><strong>Waltham Forest is the proposed first test location. It does not define the geographic scope of Unity House Centres.</strong></p>
    </article>

    <article class="card">
      <p class="eyebrow">Why start small?</p>
      <h2>Learn before considering replication</h2>
      <p>
        Pilot 01 would examine local value, resource recovery, operational reliability, safety, partner experience, evidence quality and whether another trusted host could repeat the basic process.
        The purpose is to learn whether the Unity House operating model works before considering replication elsewhere in the UK.
      </p>
      <p class="note">
        Numerical targets would be agreed after local discovery. No impact figures, savings or outcomes are being claimed in advance.
      </p>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="section boundary">
    <div class="sectionHead">
      <p class="eyebrow">Responsible development</p>
      <h2>What the current programme does not claim</h2>
      <p>
        Before any pilot could begin, host responsibilities, resource custody, food safety, insurance, safeguarding, data protection, logistics, evidence and governance would all need to be confirmed through the required readiness gates.
      </p>
      <p class="note"><strong>Unity House does not aim to replace community organisations that already work. It is being designed to connect, support and learn from existing local capability.</strong></p>
    </div>
    <div class="cards four">
      <article class="smallCard"><h3>No operating centres</h3><p>Unity House Centres is a proposed programme. No physical centre is currently operating.</p></article>
      <article class="smallCard"><h3>No fixed resource stream</h3><p>Food is proposed for Pilot 01; future nodes could use other resources where evidence and partners support them.</p></article>
      <article class="smallCard"><h3>No automated eligibility</h3><p>People would not be selected or rejected by AI, and sensitive data would be minimised.</p></article>
      <article class="smallCard"><h3>No invented proof</h3><p>Planning assumptions, synthetic records and future ambitions remain separate from real pilot evidence.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="sectionHead">
      <p class="eyebrow">Potential partner roles</p>
      <h2>Who could work with us?</h2>
      <p>
        The model is intended to connect existing capability rather than assume that one organisation can do everything. The right mix would depend on the local need, resource stream and evidence requirements.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="cards six">
      <article class="smallCard"><h3>Community hosts</h3><p>Trusted venues and local organisations able to welcome people safely.</p></article>
      <article class="smallCard"><h3>Resource partners</h3><p>Organisations able to offer suitable surplus food, essentials or other resources.</p></article>
      <article class="smallCard"><h3>Local authorities and networks</h3><p>Local knowledge, coordination and links to existing community support.</p></article>
      <article class="smallCard"><h3>Universities and evaluators</h3><p>Independent learning, measurement and responsible evidence design.</p></article>
      <article class="smallCard"><h3>Funders and support organisations</h3><p>Advice, in-kind capacity or future support where programme fit is established.</p></article>
      <article class="smallCard"><h3>Technology and innovation partners</h3><p>Simple tools for coordination and evidence, introduced only when justified.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="sectionHead">
      <p class="eyebrow">A branch of a wider vision</p>
      <h2>One branch of the Tree of Life</h2>
      <p>
        Unity House Centres is one proposed public-benefit branch of the broader Tree of Life framework. The programme could eventually connect local resource recovery with practical support, learning and opportunity—but only one branch or resource stream would be activated at a time when evidence and qualified partners justify it.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="branchGrid">
      <span>Food</span><span>Essentials</span><span>Digital</span><span>Learning</span>
      <span>Work</span><span>Repair &amp; reuse</span><span>Innovation</span><span>Evidence</span>
    </div>
    <p class="note">These are possible future branches, not a claim that all services currently exist, will launch together or belong to one operating centre.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="section supportBar">
    <div>
      <h2>What support would help at this stage?</h2>
      <p>
        The immediate need is not a large grant or a new building. We are looking for careful exploratory conversations with potential hosts,
        suitable resource partners, evaluation partners and organisations able to offer relevant in-kind knowledge or capacity for a controlled local test.
      </p>
    </div>
    <a class="btn primary" href="/contact">Contact Visio Nova Mundi</a>
  </section>

  <p class="controlNote">
    <strong>Public status:</strong> Unity House Centres is a proposed UK programme under development. No funding application, delivery, food handling, data collection, recruitment, spending, operating centre or public outcome claim is authorised by this page.
  </p>

  <style>
    .heroBlock { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.25fr .75fr; gap: 18px; align-items: start; }
    .eyebrow { margin: 0 0 9px; color: #0f766e; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .08em; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 850; }
    h1 { margin: 0 0 12px; font-size: clamp(42px, 6vw, 64px); letter-spacing: -.04em; color: var(--text); }
    .lead { margin: 0; max-width: 72ch; color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.75; font-size: 19px; }
    .actions { display: flex; gap: 12px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-top: 18px; }
    .btn { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; border-radius: 14px; padding: 11px 14px; border: 1px solid var(--border); background: white; color: var(--text); text-decoration: none; font-weight: 850; }
    .btn.primary { background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(39,99,235,.10), rgba(16,185,129,.10)); border-color: rgba(39,99,235,.25); }
    .btn:hover { border-color: rgba(0,0,0,.18); text-decoration: none; }
    .statusCard, .card, .smallCard, .supportBar { border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 18px; padding: 18px; background: white; box-shadow: 0 6px 24px rgba(0,0,0,.05); }
    .statusCard { background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(39,99,235,.07), rgba(16,185,129,.07)); }
    .statusLabel { margin: 0 0 8px; color: var(--muted); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .07em; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 850; }
    .statusCard h2, .card h2, .supportBar h2 { margin: 0 0 9px; color: var(--text); font-size: 21px; letter-spacing: -.02em; }
    .statusCard p, .card p, .smallCard p, .supportBar p { margin: 0; color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.7; }
    .statusPill { display: inline-block; margin-top: 14px; padding: 7px 10px; border-radius: 999px; border: 1px solid rgba(15,118,110,.25); color: #0f766e; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 850; }
    .section { margin-top: 34px; }
    .sectionHead h2 { margin: 0 0 8px; font-size: 29px; letter-spacing: -.025em; color: var(--text); }
    .sectionHead > p:last-child { margin: 0; max-width: 90ch; color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.75; }
    .flow { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(6, minmax(0,1fr)); gap: 10px; margin-top: 16px; }
    .flow div { display: flex; gap: 10px; align-items: center; padding: 13px; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 14px; background: rgba(39,99,235,.04); color: var(--text); font-weight: 750; }
    .flow strong { display: grid; place-items: center; flex: 0 0 28px; width: 28px; height: 28px; border-radius: 50%; background: rgba(39,99,235,.12); color: #1d4ed8; }
    .grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 14px; align-items: start; }
    .highlight { background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(39,99,235,.06), rgba(16,185,129,.06)); }
    .card ul { margin: 12px 0 0; padding-left: 18px; color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.8; }
    .note { margin-top: 12px !important; font-size: 13px; }
    .formula { margin: 14px 0 0; padding: 13px 15px; border: 1px solid rgba(15,118,110,.18); border-radius: 14px; background: rgba(16,185,129,.06); color: var(--text); line-height: 1.6; font-weight: 750; }
    .pilotFlow { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr auto 1fr auto 1fr; gap: 10px; align-items: stretch; margin-top: 16px; }
    .pilotFlow > div { display: flex; flex-direction: column; justify-content: center; gap: 5px; padding: 14px; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 14px; background: white; }
    .pilotFlow strong { color: var(--text); }
    .pilotFlow span:not(.flowArrow) { color: var(--muted); font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.55; }
    .flowArrow { align-self: center; color: #0f766e; font-size: 24px; font-weight: 850; }
    .coordinationLine { margin: 12px 0 0; padding: 11px 14px; border-left: 3px solid #0f766e; color: var(--text); background: rgba(16,185,129,.06); }
    .boundary { border-top: 1px solid var(--border); padding-top: 25px; }
    .cards.four { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0,1fr)); gap: 12px; margin-top: 14px; }
    .cards.six { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0,1fr)); gap: 12px; margin-top: 14px; }
    .smallCard { padding: 14px; }
    .smallCard h3 { margin: 0 0 7px; color: var(--text); font-size: 16px; }
    .smallCard p { font-size: 14px; }
    .branchGrid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0,1fr)); gap: 10px; margin-top: 16px; }
    .branchGrid span { padding: 12px; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 13px; background: white; color: var(--text); font-weight: 800; text-align: center; }
    .supportBar { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 18px; align-items: center; background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(39,99,235,.06), rgba(16,185,129,.06)); }
    .supportBar > div { max-width: 75ch; }
    .controlNote { margin: 18px 0 0; padding: 13px 15px; border-left: 3px solid #d97706; background: rgba(245,158,11,.09); color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.7; font-size: 13px; }
    @media (max-width: 1100px) { .flow { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0,1fr)); } }
    @media (max-width: 900px) { .heroBlock, .grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .flow, .cards.four, .cards.six { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; } .supportBar { flex-direction: column; align-items: stretch; } }
    @media (max-width: 520px) { .flow, .cards.four, .cards.six, .branchGrid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .pilotFlow { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .flowArrow { transform: rotate(90deg); } }
  </style>
</BaseLayout>
